Petrus: Third one this season.
- Then why is anyone still drawing here?
	Hope: Then why is anyone still drawing here?
	Petrus: Because the spring is forty minutes each way and this is nine.
	Petrus: You can tell a woman with three children and a full day that she should walk eighty minutes. She will listen politely.
	Petrus: The outpost has a filter now. What it does not have is anybody making sure the tablets are there when the filter has done its part.
Lindi: Filter first, then the tablets. In that order — the tablets do not work properly through muck, which is the thing nobody tells you.
Lindi: And the tablets go off. Two months, maybe a bit more. So it is not a thing you do once.
